<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Dashboards on materialize-monitoring Documentation</title><link>https://materializeinc.github.io/materialize-monitoring/preview/heather-dep-242-nodes-dashboard/dashboards/</link><description>Recent content in Dashboards on materialize-monitoring Documentation</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://materializeinc.github.io/materialize-monitoring/preview/heather-dep-242-nodes-dashboard/dashboards/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Datadog</title><link>https://materializeinc.github.io/materialize-monitoring/preview/heather-dep-242-nodes-dashboard/dashboards/datadog/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://materializeinc.github.io/materialize-monitoring/preview/heather-dep-242-nodes-dashboard/dashboards/datadog/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="datadog"&gt;Datadog&lt;a class="anchor" href="#datadog"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote class='book-hint note'&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There is no Materialize dashboard set for Datadog yet.&lt;/strong&gt;&#10;It is tracked as &lt;a href="https://linear.app/materializeinc/issue/DEP-115" rel="external nofollow" class="internal-protected-link"&gt;DEP-115&lt;/a&gt; and scheduled for &lt;strong&gt;OO-M3&lt;/strong&gt;, alongside the Google Cloud Monitoring and Honeycomb sets.&#10;See the &lt;a href="https://materializeinc.github.io/materialize-monitoring/preview/heather-dep-242-nodes-dashboard/reference/internal/roadmap/#dashboards"&gt;Dashboards workstream&lt;/a&gt; for where it sits against the rest of the work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;What exists today is the query material to build one yourself.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://materializeinc.github.io/materialize-monitoring/preview/heather-dep-242-nodes-dashboard/reference/stable-metrics/common-queries/"&gt;Common Queries&lt;/a&gt; renders every query in the registry with a &lt;strong&gt;Datadog&lt;/strong&gt; tab beside its PromQL, in the metric query syntax you paste into a dashboard widget or a monitor.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>